===Etymology 1===
From {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|elatus||lang=la|exalted, lofty, high}} {{suffix||ive|lang=en}}

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{context|grammar|lang=en}} In Semitic languages, the “adjective of superiority.” In some languages such as [[Arabic]], the concepts of [[comparative]] and [[superlative]] degree of an adjective are merged into a single form, the '''elative'''. How this form is understood or translated depends upon context and definiteness. In the absence of comparison, the elative conveys the notion of “[[greatest]]”, “[[supreme]].”
#: ''The elative of {{term|كبير||tr=kabí:r|big|lang=ar}} is {{term|اكبر|أكبر|tr=ákbar|bigger/biggest, greater/greatest|lang=ar}}.''

